    "text": "Solution Let $b$ stand for boy and $g$ for girl. The sample space of the experiment is $S = \\{(b, b), (g, b), (b, g), (g, g)\\}$\nLet E and F denote the following events :\n$E : \\text{‘both the children are boys’}$\n$F : \\text{‘at least one of the child is a boy’}$\nThen $E = \\{(b,b)\\}$ and $F = \\{(b,b), (g,b), (b,g)\\}$\nNow $E \\cap F = \\{(b,b)\\}$\nThus $P(F) = \\frac{3}{4}$ and $P(E \\cap F) = \\frac{1}{4}$\nTherefore $P(E|F) = \\frac{P(E \\cap F)}{P(F)} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{4}}{\\frac{3}{4}} = \\frac{1}{3}$",
