    },
    "chunk_index": 6
  },
  {
    "text": "The mean of a random variable does not give us information about the variability in the values of the random variable. In fact, if the variance is small, then the values of the random variable are close to the mean. Also random variables with different probability distributions can have equal means, as shown in the following distributions of X and Y.",
    "page_number": 3,
    "metadata": {
      "source_url": "page_3.png",
      "source_type": "image",
      "topics": [
        "probability",
        "random variables"
      ],
      "subtopics": [
        "variance",
        "mean",
        "variability"
      ],
      "chunk_type": "explanation",
      "difficulty_level": "basic",
      "prerequisites": [
        "expectation",
        "probability distribution"
      ]
    },
    "chunk_index": 7
  },
  {
